\"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"SCE\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 68322, \"displayName\": \"Saccharomyces cerevisiae\", \"name\": [\"Saccharomyces cerevisiae\", \"S.cerevisiae\", \"S. cerevisiae\", \"Sc\", \"baker's yeast\", \"brewer's yeast\", \"Saccharomyces cerevisiae (strain RM11-1a)\", \"Saccharomyces cerevisiae (strain YJM789)\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"4932\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Saccharomyces cerevisiae\", \"stId\": \"R-SCE-1675994\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SCE-1675994.1\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9990864, \"displayName\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome